From: DevCon Training <devcon@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] lvgl: do not claim tiled image tasks when the GPU lacks pattern repeat

Tiled images are drawn with VG_LITE_PATTERN_REPEAT. On GPUs that do not
implement repeat/reflect the blit is rejected and every tiled frame falls
back after a failed submission. Decline the task during evaluation so the
software renderer takes it directly.

---
diff --git a/src/draw/vg_lite/lv_draw_vg_lite.c b/src/draw/vg_lite/lv_draw_vg_lite.c
index 1cf567589..031e5c49b 100644
--- a/src/draw/vg_lite/lv_draw_vg_lite.c
+++ b/src/draw/vg_lite/lv_draw_vg_lite.c
@@ -94,6 +94,12 @@ void lv_draw_vg_lite_deinit(void)
 
 static bool check_image_is_supported(const lv_draw_image_dsc_t * dsc)
 {
+    /* Tiled images are drawn as a repeat pattern. GPUs without repeat/reflect
+     * support reject the blit, so leave those tasks to the software renderer. */
+    if(dsc->tile && !vg_lite_query_feature(gcFEATURE_BIT_VG_IM_REPEAT_REFLECT)) {
+        return false;
+    }
+
     return lv_vg_lite_is_src_cf_supported(dsc->header.cf);
 }
 
